Appendix B: Functional Derivative of the Regularized Alignment Functional

This appendix derives the functional derivative of \mathcal{A}_\mu and verifies the cancellation of the spurious +1 term that appeared in earlier revisions.

B.1 Setup

Let \Psi\in H^1(\Omega\times\Theta) with \Psi\ge 0, and fix a mollifier \mu\in L^\infty_+(\Theta) with \mu\ge\mu_{\min}>0. Define

\rho_\mu(\mathbf{x})=\int_\Theta(\Psi+\mu)\,d\mu_\Theta,\qquad p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}(\theta)=\frac{\Psi(\mathbf{x},\theta)+\mu(\theta)}{\rho_\mu(\mathbf{x})},\qquad \mathcal{V}_\mu=\frac{\mathcal{V}+\mu}{\|\mathcal{V}+\mu\|_1}.
\tag{B.1}

The regularized alignment functional is

\mathcal{A}_\mu(\Psi,\mathcal{V})=\int_\Omega w(\mathbf{x})\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}\,\Big\|\,\mathcal{V}_\mu\right)d\mathbf{x}.
\tag{B.2}

B.2 First Variation

Let \delta\Psi\in H^1 be a variation. Then \delta\rho_\mu=\int_\Theta\delta\Psi\,d\mu_\Theta, and

\delta p^{(\mu)}=\frac{\delta\Psi-p^{(\mu)}\delta\rho_\mu}{\rho_\mu}.
\tag{B.3}

The first variation of D_{\mathrm{KL}} is

\delta D_{\mathrm{KL}}=\int_\Theta\delta p^{(\mu)}\left(\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}+1\right)d\mu_\Theta.
\tag{B.4}

Substituting (B.3),

\delta D_{\mathrm{KL}}=\frac{1}{\rho_\mu}\int_\Theta\delta\Psi\left(\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}+1\right)d\mu_\Theta-\frac{\delta\rho_\mu}{\rho_\mu}\int_\Theta p^{(\mu)}\left(\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}+1\right)d\mu_\Theta.
\tag{B.5}

Using \int_\Theta p^{(\mu)}\,d\mu_\Theta=1 and \int_\Theta p^{(\mu)}\log(p^{(\mu)}/\mathcal{V}_\mu)\,d\mu_\Theta=D_{\mathrm{KL}},

\int_\Theta p^{(\mu)}\left(\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}+1\right)d\mu_\Theta=D_{\mathrm{KL}}+1.
\tag{B.6}

Therefore

\delta D_{\mathrm{KL}}=\frac{1}{\rho_\mu}\int_\Theta\delta\Psi\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}\,d\mu_\Theta+\frac{\delta\rho_\mu}{\rho_\mu}-\frac{\delta\rho_\mu}{\rho_\mu}(D_{\mathrm{KL}}+1)=\frac{1}{\rho_\mu}\int_\Theta\delta\Psi\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}\,d\mu_\Theta-\frac{\delta\rho_\mu}{\rho_\mu}D_{\mathrm{KL}}.
\tag{B.7}

The two \delta\rho_\mu/\rho_\mu terms cancel: the +1 from the variation of the log term cancels the -1 inside the normalization contribution. Substituting \delta\rho_\mu=\int_\Theta\delta\Psi\,d\mu_\Theta,

\delta D_{\mathrm{KL}}=\int_\Theta\frac{\delta\Psi}{\rho_\mu}\left[\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}}{\mathcal{V}_\mu}-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\right]d\mu_\Theta.
\tag{B.8}

Multiplying by w(\mathbf{x}) and integrating over \Omega,

\delta\mathcal{A}_\mu=\int_\Omega\int_\Theta\frac{w(\mathbf{x})}{\rho_\mu(\mathbf{x})}\left[\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}(\theta)}{\mathcal{V}_\mu(\theta)}-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}\,\Big\|\,\mathcal{V}_\mu\right)\right]\delta\Psi(\mathbf{x},\theta)\,d\mu_\Theta(\theta)\,d\mathbf{x}.
\tag{B.9}

Hence

\frac{\delta\mathcal{A}_\mu}{\delta\Psi}(\mathbf{x},\theta)=\frac{w(\mathbf{x})}{\rho_\mu(\mathbf{x})}\left[\log\frac{p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}(\theta)}{\mathcal{V}_\mu(\theta)}-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}\,\Big\|\,\mathcal{V}_\mu\right)\right].
\tag{B.10}

B.3 Consistency Checks

Check 1 (Vanishing at the reference). If p^{(\mu)}_{\mathbf{x}}=\mathcal{V}_\mu for all \mathbf{x}, then D_{\mathrm{KL}}=0 and \log(p^{(\mu)}/\mathcal{V}_\mu)=0, so \delta\mathcal{A}_\mu/\delta\Psi=0 identically.

Check 2 (Sign of the prior revision's error). The prior revision displayed \delta\mathcal{A}/\delta\Psi=w[\log(p/\mathcal{V})+1-D_{\mathrm{KL}}]/\rho. The +1 is spurious: it cancels against the normalization contribution from \rho_\mu, as shown in (B.7). With the +1 retained, the derivative would not vanish at p^{(\mu)}=\mathcal{V}_\mu, contradicting the fact that \mathcal{A}_\mu attains its minimum there.

Check 3 (Limiting behaviour as \mu\to 0). On the set \{\Psi\ge\delta_{\min}\}, \rho_\mu\to\rho and p^{(\mu)}\to p uniformly, so \delta\mathcal{A}_\mu/\delta\Psi\to\delta\mathcal{A}/\delta\Psi in L^\infty. The constants appearing in the hypotheses of Appendix E depend on \mu_{\min} and on \delta_{\min}; this dependence is not tracked explicitly and should be understood throughout.

