Appendix F: Thermodynamic Consistency and Corrected Sign Convention

This appendix documents the sign correction in the reaction entropy production and records the scope of the geometric decomposition cited.

F.1 Gradient Structure Hypothesis (H-TH)

There exists a convex, coercive C^1 functional \mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}:H^1\to\mathbb{R} with unique minimizer \Psi^*, such that

F_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi)=-\nabla_\Psi\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi).
\tag{F.1}

F.2 Corrected Reaction Entropy Production

Definition F.1. Under (F.1),

\sigma_{\mathrm{react}}=-\frac{1}{T}\left\langle F_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi)-F_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi^*),\,\Psi-\Psi^*\right\rangle.
\tag{F.2}

Proposition F.2. Under (H-TH), \sigma_{\mathrm{react}}\ge 0.

Proof. Substituting (F.1),

\sigma_{\mathrm{react}}=\frac{1}{T}\left\langle\nabla\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi)-\nabla\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi^*),\,\Psi-\Psi^*\right\rangle.
\tag{F.3}

By monotonicity of the gradient of a convex functional, the right-hand side is non-negative. \square

F.3 Sign Error in Prior Revision

The prior revision displayed

\sigma_{\mathrm{react}}=\frac{1}{T}\left(F_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi)-F_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi^*)\right)(\Psi-\Psi^*).
\tag{F.4}

Under (H-TH), this equals

-\frac{1}{T}\left\langle\nabla\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi)-\nabla\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{BUDT}}(\Psi^*),\,\Psi-\Psi^*\right\rangle\le 0,
\tag{F.5}

which is non-positive and contradicts the claimed non-negativity. The sign convention (F.2) resolves the inconsistency.

F.4 Scope of the Geometric Decomposition

The decomposition

\sigma=\sigma_{\mathrm{diff}}+\sigma_{\mathrm{react}}+\sigma_{\mathrm{cross}}
\tag{F.6}

with \sigma_{\mathrm{diff}}=(D/T)|\nabla\Psi|^2 is a modelling choice adapted from the out-of-equilibrium thermodynamics literature. The precise form used here is not a direct consequence of the Kolchinsky–Ito decomposition (Phys. Rev. Research 4, L012034, 2022), which is stated for discrete Markov jump systems and does not contain reaction–diffusion PDE formulas. We retain (F.6) as a modelling ansatz; its derivation from a microscopic stochastic model for the field \Psi is an open problem.

F.5 Total Entropy Production

Corollary F.3. Under (H-TH) and \sigma_{\mathrm{cross}}=0, \sigma\ge 0.

The cross term \sigma_{\mathrm{cross}} is assumed to vanish when thermodynamic forces are orthogonal; this is a hypothesis on the reaction–diffusion structure of the field equation, not a derived property.

