Appendix I: Kleisli Composition Bound

I.1 Setup

Let \mathcal{P} be the Giry monad on \mathbf{Meas}. An alignment-enriched cognitive module is a pair (k,\alpha) with k:X\to\mathcal{P}(Y) a Markov kernel and \alpha:X\to\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} measurable, satisfying

D_{\mathrm{KL}}(k(\cdot|x)\|\mathcal{V}_Y)\le\alpha(x)\quad\text{for all }x\in X.
\tag{I.1}

I.2 Composition

For (k,\alpha):X\to Y and (\ell,\beta):Y\to Z, the composite is (\ell\circ_K k,\gamma) with

(\ell\circ_K k)(dz|x)=\int_Y\ell(dz|y)k(dy|x),\qquad\gamma(x)=\int_Y\beta(y)k(dy|x).
\tag{I.2}

I.3 Composition Theorem

Theorem I.1. If (k,\alpha):X\to Y and (\ell,\beta):Y\to Z are alignment-enriched modules, then

D_{\mathrm{KL}}((\ell\circ_K k)(\cdot|x)\|\mathcal{V}_Z)\le\gamma(x)
\tag{I.3}

for all x\in X.

Proof. Write q(dz|x)=\int_Y\ell(dz|y)k(dy|x). Then

D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\|\mathcal{V}_Z)=\int_Z\left(\int_Y\ell(z|y)k(dy|x)\right)\log\frac{\int_Y\ell(z|y')k(dy'|x)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)}\,dz.
\tag{I.4}

Apply Jensen's inequality to the convex function u\mapsto u\log(u/\mathcal{V}_Z(z)) for each fixed z:

\left(\int_Y\ell(z|y)k(dy|x)\right)\log\frac{\int_Y\ell(z|y')k(dy'|x)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)}\le\int_Y\ell(z|y)\log\frac{\ell(z|y)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)}\,k(dy|x).
\tag{I.5}

Integrating over z and applying Fubini,

D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\|\mathcal{V}_Z)\le\int_Y\left(\int_Z\ell(z|y)\log\frac{\ell(z|y)}{\mathcal{V}_Z(z)}\,dz\right)k(dy|x)=\int_Y D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\ell(\cdot|y)\|\mathcal{V}_Z)\,k(dy|x)\le\int_Y\beta(y)k(dy|x)=\gamma(x).
\tag{I.6}

\square

Remark I.2. The prior revision used a non-standard "chain rule" for KL divergence (KL is not multiplicative under composition). The correct estimate is Jensen's inequality above. The resulting bound is strictly stronger: the term \alpha(x) from the prior revision's bound is unnecessary.

Remark I.3. Measurability of \gamma follows from measurability of k and \beta. Associativity follows from associativity of the Giry monad.

